th magnetic lows, low-resistivity, and low-chargeability responses, whereas magnetite-bearing alteration produces magnetic highs. Zones of intense quartz-illite alteration and silicification corres"},{"page":47,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"The surveys identified several northeast- and northwest-trending fault systems, magnetic anomalies associated with intrusive rocks, and zones of quartz, silicification, and argillic alteration."},{"page":49,"explained":false,"untested":true,"text":"The programme included four deep IP/resistivity profiles (investigation depth of 650\u2013700 m) and three shallow profiles (investigation depth of 220\u2013250 m)."}]},"rock":{"density_samples":{"n":1,"min":199.0,"max":199.0,"median":199.0,"page":100,"text":"occurred at any chosen parameters 14.10 Bulk Density LE collected 199 bulk density measurements from 16 drill holes using the water immersion technique."},"density_low":{"n":1,"min":2.02,"max":2.02,"median":2.02,"page":101,"text":"\u00a9 SLR Consulting LLC 2026 The bulk density values range from 2.02 t/m3 to 2.92 t/m3 and are normally distributed about a mean of 2.63 t/m3."},"density_high":{"n":1,"min":2.92,"max":2.92,"median":2.92,"page":101,"text":"\u00a9 SLR Consulting LLC 2026 The bulk density values range from 2.02 t/m3 to 2.92 t/m3 and are normally distributed about a mean of 2.63 t/m3."},"density":{"n":1,"min":2.02,"max":2.02,"median":2.02,"page":101,"text":"\u00a9 SLR Consulting LLC 2026 The bulk density values range from 2.02 t/m3 to 2.92 t/m3 and are normally distributed about a mean of 2.63 t/m3."},"slope_angle_deg":{"n":1,"min":50.0,"max":50.0,"median":50.0,"page":110,"text":"A pit slope angle of 50\u00b0 and a bench height of 10 m were used in the optimisation."}},"model_params":{"block":[10.0,10.0,5.0],"composite_m":1.0,"radius_m":40.0,"default_cutoff":0.15,"method":"idw","power":2.0,"metallurgy":{"routes":["cil_cip"],"traits":["sulphide","arsenic"],"recoveries":null,"summary":"sulphide ore, arsenic-beari